---
import Page from "../components/Page.astro";
---

<Page page="About" , site="Simulating Nature">
  <section class="container">
    <img class="profile__photo" src="https://placehold.co/400x300/png" alt="" />
    <p>
      The main goal of this personal blog is to collect, synthesize, and
      preserve various useful or intriguing discoveries I encounter in my daily
      life. While my main focus lies in the numerical simulation of physical
      processes, I am also interested computer algebra/proof systems.
    </p>
    <p>
      A secondary objective is to foster interactive discussions on social media
      —maybe on Mastodon, someday— where insights can be shared, refined, and
      expanded to a wider audience.
    </p>
    <p>
      I am also a strong advocate of reproducible research and believe in
      accessible scientific data and methodologies. At some point, I might
      maintain notes about how I package code with research papers (it evolves
      quickly).
    </p>
    <h2>Academic position</h2>
    <p>
      I am currently a postdoctoral researcher in the <a
        href="https://www.ige-grenoble.fr/-OPERA-">OPERA</a
      > team at <a href="https://www.ige-grenoble.fr/"
        >Institut des Géosciences de l'Environnement (IGE)</a
      >, Grenoble, France. I am working on new numerical schemes for global
      ocean circulation models using machine learning.
    </p>
  </section>
</Page>

<style>
  .profile__photo {
    max-width: 100%;
  }
</style>
